-- title:
--   Local normal form of an idele in the Tₚ Hecke set
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be negative rationals and $q'$ a natural number such that the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L87), i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ is a unit precisely when $q'\in w$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ that is an Eichler order of level $N$, meaning $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ with relative index $[\Lambda_1:R]=N$. Let $p$ be a prime and $v$ a height-one prime with $p\in v$, $q'\notin v$ and $N\notin v$. Let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ lying in `primeHeckeSet R p`, that is: $n$ and $p\cdot n^{-1}$ lie in the additive group `finiteAdeleBox R` generated by the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adele, while $n^{-1}$ and $p^{-1}\cdot n$ do not. Then (i) for every height-one prime $w\neq v$, the images of $n$ and of $n^{-1}$ under [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36) at $w$ lie in [`Submodule.localBox R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), the additive group generated by the $z\otimes c$ with $z\in R$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_w$; and (ii) there is a ring isomorphism $\varphi:\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v\to M_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ with $\varphi(1\otimes r)=r\cdot 1$ for all $r\in\mathbb{Q}_v$, carrying [`Submodule.localBox R v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) exactly onto the matrices with all entries in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$, together with mutually inverse matrices $k_0,k_0^{\mathrm{i}}$ with all entries in that valuation ring, such that the $v$-component of $n$ has $\varphi$-image $\mathrm{diag}(1,p)\,k_0$ and the $v$-component of $n^{-1}$ has $\varphi$-image $k_0^{\mathrm{i}}\,\mathrm{diag}(1,p^{-1})$.
--
--   This is the local normal form underlying the Hecke operator $T_p$ on an Eichler order at a prime $p$ not dividing the level and distinct from the ramified prime: the $p$-component of such an idele has elementary divisors $(1,p)$ in a matrix model in which the order becomes $M_2(\mathbb{Z}_p)$, while all other components are units of the corresponding local orders. It is used in the Čeredník–Drinfeld class-set tower constructions, where the intersection order attached to such an idele is shown to be Eichler of the expected level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_exists_ringEquiv_localBox_iff_evalAt_eq_diagonal_mul_of_mem_primeHeckeSet.lean

